_at":"2026-10-14T14:50:48.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110382823332855881"],"entities":{"hashtags":[{"end":31,"start":24,"tag":"Texans"}],"urls":[{"display_url":"x.com/HoustonTexans/…","end":58,"expanded_url":"https://twitter.com/HoustonTexans/status/2110381826791333952","start":35,"url":"https://t.co/gaYNJmHXxa"}]},"id":"2110382823332855881","lang":"en","possibly_sensitive":false,"public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":12,"impression_count":253318,"like_count":644,"quote_count":2,"reply_count":15,"repost_count":33},"referenced_tweets":[{"id":"2110381826791333952","type":"quoted"}],"text":"Help on the way for the #Texans... https://t.co/gaYNJmHXxa","url":"https://x.com/RapSheet/status/2110382823332855881"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["13_2110228451345002496"]},"author_id":"1893606127834738688","conversation_id":"2110228564717015082","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:37:50.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110228564717015082"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/k6Zcz2ftgf","end":298,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/GigglingGanon/status/2110228564717015082/video/1","media_key":"13_2110228451345002496","start":275,"url":"https://t.co/k6Zcz2ftgf"},{"display_url":"x.com/GigglingGanon/…","end":322,"expanded_url":"https://twitter.com/GigglingGanon/status/2110202191373828373","start":299,"url":"https://t.co/NGDA0UCVOZ"}]},"id":"2110228564717015082","lang":"en","note_tweet":{"text":"These CPS officers have never had anyone crush their narrative like this all while giving them nothing back in return. \n\n​Two Child Protective Services caseworkers show up at a resident’s front door alleging that threats were made against a family court judge via voicemail. Instead of allowing the confrontation to turn into an informal interrogation, the homeowner shuts down the inquiry at the threshold.\n\n​Here is the breakdown of why this encounter is a must see and what it reveals about administrative investigations.\n\n​Jurisdictional Realities vs. Bureaucratic Overreach: As the resident immediately points out, CPS is not a criminal law enforcement agency. If credible, actionable threats had truly been uttered against a judicial officer months prior, the RCMP or local law enforcement would have arrived with an arrest warrant, not social workers conducting an unscheduled fishing expedition.\n\n​Refusal to Self-Incriminate & \"Contracting\": When the caseworker attempts to probe into his mental health, the resident firmly refuses to engage, noting he has already undergone an official court assessment that cleared him completely. By keeping the document sealed and refusing to \"contract\" or answer unprompted questions, he denies the agency the opportunity to extract statements that could be twisted, decontextualized, and used against him in family court filings.\n\n​Protecting the Curtilage & Enforcing Formal Trespass: Without an active warrant or an exigent emergency involving the immediate safety of a child, caseworkers have no greater legal authority to remain on private property than any standard solicitor.\n\n The homeowner repeatedly exercises his property rights, orders them to leave, and places the caseworkers on formal trespass notice the moment they step beyond his property boundary.\n\nWhen government representatives show up without warrants, vague accusations can easily turn into self-inflicted legal traps if you do not understand where their authority ends and your rights begin. Your rights are like your muscles, if you fail to exercise them, they will fade away."},"possibly_sensitive":false,"public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":1848,"impression_count":239386,"like_count":7961,"quote_count":88,"reply_count":543,"repost_count":1522},"referenced_tweets":[{"id":"2110202191373828373","type":"quoted"}],"text":"These CPS officers have never had anyone crush their narrative like this all while giving them nothing back in return. \n\n​Two Child Protective Services caseworkers show up at a resident’s front door alleging that threats were made agai